  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: Build a polished, production-quality web app called **Personal Gemini Journal** \342\200\224 a private space where users can put *anything* on their mind: thoughts, ideas, worries, plans, decisions, goals, or random notes.\n\nThe core experience is:\n\n> **Write freely \342\206\222 Gemini helps organize it \342\206\222 understand it \342\206\222 connect it to previous thoughts.**\n\nThis should feel like a **beautiful modern journal + intelligent thinking space**, not a generic chatbot.\n\n### Core experience\n\n* Firebase Google authentication with strictly private, user-isolated Firestore data.\n* A calm, premium journal interface where users can immediately start writing without choosing categories or filling forms.\n* Autosave journal entries and maintain a searchable history.\n* After writing, offer **\342\200\234Make sense of this\342\200\235** \342\200\224 Gemini analyzes the entry and gently surfaces:\n\n  * key thoughts\n  * themes\n  * questions\n  * ideas\n  * decisions\n  * possible next steps\n* Let users have a contextual, multi-turn conversation with Gemini about any entry.\n* Gemini should **organize and reflect, not dominate**: ask thoughtful questions, identify possibilities and connections, and never present assumptions as facts.\n* Over time, connect related entries and surface recurring themes, unfinished thoughts, and relevant older reflections.\n* Include an **Insights** view showing meaningful patterns across the user\'s journal.\n* Include optional **user-controlled memory**: Gemini can suggest something to remember, but the user must approve it. Memories must be viewable, editable, and deletable.\n\n### UI/UX\n\nMake the experience exceptionally beautiful, calm, and interactive \342\200\224 **premium writing app + personal knowledge space + AI reflection layer**.\n\nUse elegant typography, generous whitespace, subtle animations, thoughtful microinteractions, excellent empty/loading/error states, and a responsive mobile experience.\n\nAvoid generic AI aesthetics, excessive cards, dashboards, purple gradients, giant AI avatars, and unnecessary gamification.\n\n### Security\n\nUse Firebase Authentication + Cloud Firestore with strict security rules so users can only access their own data. Keep Gemini credentials server-side using appropriate environment variables/Secret Manager. Never expose API keys in client code.\n\n### Critical requirement\n\nDo not build **\342\200\234a chatbot that saves conversations.\342\200\235**\n\nBuild:\n\n> **\342\200\234A private place where I can put everything in my head, and Gemini helps me turn that mess into clarity.\342\200\235**\n\nFirst make this end-to-end flow excellent:\n\n**Sign in \342\206\222 write anything \342\206\222 save \342\206\222 \342\200\234Make sense of this\342\200\235 \342\206\222 discuss with Gemini \342\206\222 revisit later \342\206\222 discover connections.**\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.eslintrc.json\n/.gitignore\n/app/globals.css\n/app/layout.tsx\n/eslint.config.mjs\n/hooks/use-mobile.ts\n/lib/utils.ts\n/metadata.json\n/next-env.d.ts\n/next.config.ts\n/package.json\n/postcss.config.mjs\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/tsconfig.json\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@hookform/resolvers: ^5.2.1\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nclass-variance-authority: ^0.7.1\nclsx: ^2.1.1\nlucide-react: ^0.553.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nnext: ^15.4.9\npostcss: ^8.5.6\nreact: ^19.2.1\nreact-dom: ^19.2.1\ntailwind-merge: ^3.3.1\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@tailwindcss/postcss: 4.1.11\n@tailwindcss/typography: ^0.5.19\n@types/node: ^20\n@types/react: ^19\n@types/react-dom: ^19\neslint: 9.39.1\neslint-config-next: 16.0.8\nfirebase-tools: ^15.0.0\ntailwindcss: 4.1.11\ntw-animate-css: ^1.4.0\ntypescript: 5.9.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /app/globals.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /app/layout.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport type {Metadata} from \'next\';\nimport \'./globals.css\'; // Global styles\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n  description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n  openGraph: {\n    title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n    description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n    type: \'website\',\n  },\n  twitter: {\n    card: \'summary_large_image\',\n    title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n    description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n  },\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({children}: {children: React.ReactNode}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body suppressHydrationWarning>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /next.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport type {NextConfig} from \'next\';\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n  reactStrictMode: true,\n  eslint: {\n    ignoreDuringBuilds: true,\n  },\n  typescript: {\n    ignoreBuildErrors: false,\n  },\n  // Allow access to remote image placeholder.\n  images: {\n    remotePatterns: [\n      {\n        protocol: \'https\',\n        hostname: \'picsum.photos\',\n        port: \'\',\n        pathname: \'/**\', // This allows any path under the hostname\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  output: \'standalone\',\n  transpilePackages: [\'motion\'],\n  webpack: (config, {dev}) => {\n    // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n    // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n    if (dev && process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\') {\n      config.watchOptions = {\n        ignored: /.*/,\n      };\n    }\n    return config;\n  },\n};\n\nexport default nextConfig;\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"next\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"baseUrl\": \".\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\"./*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: Build a polished, production-quality web app called **Personal Gemini Journal** \342\200\224 a private space where users can put *anything* on their mind: thoughts, ideas, worries, plans, decisions, goals, or random notes.\n\nThe core experience is:\n\n> **Write freely \342\206\222 Gemini helps organize it \342\206\222 understand it \342\206\222 connect it to previous thoughts.**\n\nThis should feel like a **beautiful modern journal + intelligent thinking space**, not a generic chatbot.\n\n### Core experience\n\n* Firebase Google authentication with strictly private, user-isolated Firestore data.\n* A calm, premium journal interface where users can immediately start writing without choosing categories or filling forms.\n* Autosave journal entries and maintain a searchable history.\n* After writing, offer **\342\200\234Make sense of this\342\200\235** \342\200\224 Gemini analyzes the entry and gently surfaces:\n\n  * key thoughts\n  * themes\n  * questions\n  * ideas\n  * decisions\n  * possible next steps\n* Let users have a contextual, multi-turn conversation with Gemini about any entry.\n* Gemini should **organize and reflect, not dominate**: ask thoughtful questions, identify possibilities and connections, and never present assumptions as facts.\n* Over time, connect related entries and surface recurring themes, unfinished thoughts, and relevant older reflections.\n* Include an **Insights** view showing meaningful patterns across the user\'s journal.\n* Include optional **user-controlled memory**: Gemini can suggest something to remember, but the user must approve it. Memories must be viewable, editable, and deletable.\n\n### UI/UX\n\nMake the experience exceptionally beautiful, calm, and interactive \342\200\224 **premium writing app + personal knowledge space + AI reflection layer**.\n\nUse elegant typography, generous whitespace, subtle animations, thoughtful microinteractions, excellent empty/loading/error states, and a responsive mobile experience.\n\nAvoid generic AI aesthetics, excessive cards, dashboards, purple gradients, giant AI avatars, and unnecessary gamification.\n\n### Security\n\nUse Firebase Authentication + Cloud Firestore with strict security rules so users can only access their own data. Keep Gemini credentials server-side using appropriate environment variables/Secret Manager. Never expose API keys in client code.\n\n### Critical requirement\n\nDo not build **\342\200\234a chatbot that saves conversations.\342\200\235**\n\nBuild:\n\n> **\342\200\234A private place where I can put everything in my head, and Gemini helps me turn that mess into clarity.\342\200\235**\n\nFirst make this end-to-end flow excellent:\n\n**Sign in \342\206\222 write anything \342\206\222 save \342\206\222 \342\200\234Make sense of this\342\200\235 \342\206\222 discuss with Gemini \342\206\222 revisit later \342\206\222 discover connections.**\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.eslintrc.json\n/.gitignore\n/app/globals.css\n/app/layout.tsx\n/eslint.config.mjs\n/hooks/use-mobile.ts\n/lib/utils.ts\n/metadata.json\n/next-env.d.ts\n/next.config.ts\n/package.json\n/postcss.config.mjs\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/tsconfig.json\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@hookform/resolvers: ^5.2.1\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nclass-variance-authority: ^0.7.1\nclsx: ^2.1.1\nlucide-react: ^0.553.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nnext: ^15.4.9\npostcss: ^8.5.6\nreact: ^19.2.1\nreact-dom: ^19.2.1\ntailwind-merge: ^3.3.1\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@tailwindcss/postcss: 4.1.11\n@tailwindcss/typography: ^0.5.19\n@types/node: ^20\n@types/react: ^19\n@types/react-dom: ^19\neslint: 9.39.1\neslint-config-next: 16.0.8\nfirebase-tools: ^15.0.0\ntailwindcss: 4.1.11\ntw-animate-css: ^1.4.0\ntypescript: 5.9.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /app/globals.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /app/layout.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport type {Metadata} from \'next\';\nimport \'./globals.css\'; // Global styles\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n  description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n  openGraph: {\n    title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n    description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n    type: \'website\',\n  },\n  twitter: {\n    card: \'summary_large_image\',\n    title: \'My Google AI Studio App\',\n    description: \'An application built with Google AI Studio.\',\n  },\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({children}: {children: React.ReactNode}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body suppressHydrationWarning>{children}</body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /next.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport type {NextConfig} from \'next\';\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n  reactStrictMode: true,\n  eslint: {\n    ignoreDuringBuilds: true,\n  },\n  typescript: {\n    ignoreBuildErrors: false,\n  },\n  // Allow access to remote image placeholder.\n  images: {\n    remotePatterns: [\n      {\n        protocol: \'https\',\n        hostname: \'picsum.photos\',\n        port: \'\',\n        pathname: \'/**\', // This allows any path under the hostname\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  output: \'standalone\',\n  transpilePackages: [\'motion\'],\n  webpack: (config, {dev}) => {\n    // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n    // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n    if (dev && process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\') {\n      config.watchOptions = {\n        ignored: /.*/,\n      };\n    }\n    return config;\n  },\n};\n\nexport default nextConfig;\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2017\",\n    \"lib\": [\"dom\", \"dom.iterable\", \"esnext\"],\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true,\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"module\": \"esnext\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"preserve\",\n    \"incremental\": true,\n    \"plugins\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"next\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"baseUrl\": \".\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\"./*\"]\n    }\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"next-env.d.ts\", \"**/*.ts\", \"**/*.tsx\", \".next/types/**/*.ts\"],\n  \"exclude\": [\"node_modules\"]\n}\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
