ck` function, taking content and config, to use the model ladder: `\"gemini-3.6-flash\"`, then `\"gemini-3.1-flash-lite\"`, then dynamic alias `\"gemini-flash-latest\"`, and then `\"gemini-2.5-flash\"` or the Deep Reasoning Model.\n\n\n**Defining Model Prioritization**\n\nI\'m now refining the model selection. I\'ve defined a `MODELS` constant array, prioritizing models. I\'m focusing on \"gemini-2.5-flash,\" then \"gemini-2.5-pro\", and adding the prioritized list of models from earlier. Next, I\'m working on the `generateContentWithFallback` helper function, which will cycle through these models in a loop, handling errors. I need to make sure I am doing the model fallbacks properly, and logging appropriately. I am now working on the error handling and iteration logic.\n\\n\\n\nI\'ve pivoted to consider structured output for the \"Make sense of this\" analysis. I\'m exploring structured output options within the `@google/genai` library, specifically the `responseMimeType` and `responseSchema` configuration. I\'m evaluating the use of JSON schema to ensure Gemini returns structured JSON responses consistently, while considering potential edge cases.\n\n\n"
