  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///README.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "# Personal Gemini Journal\n\nA beautiful, private thinking space and reflective journal powered by Google Cloud, Firebase Authentication, and Gemini fallback ladders. This application acts as an intelligent sounding board to help users organize, connect, and clarify their thoughts without exposing API secrets in browser clients.\n\n---\n\n## Technical Architecture\n\n- **Frontend**: Next.js 15+ App Router, Tailwind CSS, and `motion` (Framer Motion) microinteractions.\n- **Backend Service**: Unified server routes validating JSON payloads and authenticating authorization headers.\n- **Database**: Strictly private, owner-isolated Google Cloud Firestore.\n- **Cognitive Layer**: Modern `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK executing a resilient fallback loop over dynamic model ladders:\n  - Primary: `gemini-3.6-flash`\n  - High-Availability: `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`\n  - Dynamic Alias: `gemini-flash-latest`\n  - Deep Reasoning: `gemini-3.7-flash`\n\n---\n\n## Security Zones\n\n1. **User Data Isolation**: Access control is enforced at the database level. Users can only perform CRUD operations on their own documents.\n2. **Secret Management**: Server-side credentials (like `GEMINI_API_KEY`) are kept on the server and are never sent to the browser.\n3. **Defense in Depth**: Defensive schema checks and null-safe deserialization in API routes prevent query injection and unexpected runtime failures.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Firebase Firestore Security Configuration\n\nCreate a `firestore.rules` file in your repository with the owner-bound isolation rule block:\n\n```javascript\nrules_version = \'2\';\nservice cloud.firestore {\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\n    match /users/{userId} {\n      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;\n      \n      match /{document=**} {\n        allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDeploy the rules securely using Firebase CLI:\n```bash\nfirebase deploy --only firestore:rules\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Cloud Secret Manager Integration\n\nEnsure that the default Cloud Run Compute Service Account or your custom service account has the necessary Secret Manager Accessor permissions.\n\n```bash\n# Create the secret holding your API Key\ngcloud secrets create GEMINI_API_KEY --replication-policy=\"automatic\"\necho -n \"YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY\" | gcloud secrets versions add GEMINI_API_KEY --data-file=-\n\n# Grant Secret Manager Secret Accessor role to the Cloud Run runtime service account\ngcloud secrets add-iam-policy-binding GEMINI_API_KEY \\\n  --member=\"serviceAccount:YOUR_PROJECT_NUMBER-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com\" \\\n  --role=\"roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Unified Production Deployment (Cloud Run)\n\nCompile the standalone build and deploy the container service to Google Cloud Run:\n\n```bash\n# Build the Next.js production standalone package\nnpm run build\n\n# Deploy the service directly from sources\ngcloud run deploy personal-gemini-journal \\\n  --source=. \\\n  --region=us-central1 \\\n  --allow-unauthenticated \\\n  --set-secrets=GEMINI_API_KEY=GEMINI_API_KEY:latest \\\n  --update-labels=dev-tutorial=cloud-run-ai-challenge\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Local Development\n\nCopy and configure your local environmental settings:\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env.local\n```\n\nPopulate the local credentials inside `.env.local`:\n```env\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"AIzaSy...\"\n```\n\nLaunch the hot-reloading development server:\n```bash\nnpm run dev\n```\n"
    }
