    thinking: "**Defining the Core Product**\n\nOkay, the concept has crystallized! The product\'s new name is **Sanjaya**, and it\'s no longer just a journal. I am focusing on its role as a personal witness: \"You live the story. Sanjaya helps you see it.\" This subtle shift is key!\n\n\n**Mapping the Technical Landscape**\n\nI am now taking stock of the available skills to implement the \"Sanjaya\" architecture. I can leverage `firebase-integration` and `gemini-api`, focusing on the core \"capture, structure, connect, reflect, discover\" loop. I have reviewed the requirements, and I will be proceeding with implementation, after some adjustments to the `metadata.json` name and description.\n\n\n**Refining the AI Witness**\n\nI am working on the AI\'s persona, it should be a witness, not a therapist. It will be grounded solely on past text to highlight patterns or contradictions. The HTML title will be updated to \"Sanjaya \342\200\224 Personal Journal & Witness.\" I\'m also now thinking deeply about the four core tabs: Home, My Story, Connections, and Discover. The initial approach will focus on elegantly capturing input.\n\n\n"
