  planner_response {
    response: "I will edit `/app/api/gemini/analyze/route.ts` to implement Sanjaya\'s distinct AI behavior rules. It will operate purely as an objective witness to the user\'s life story, avoiding motivational coaching or clinical diagnoses. It will extract lightweight structured cards (`Thought`, `Idea`, `Question`, `Decision`, `Goal`, `Moment`, `Person`, `Pattern`), synthesize an elegant witness reflection, and detect relationships to previous entries."
    thinking: "**Considering Implementation**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a handle on the current architecture. My focus has shifted to the changes required for Sanjaya. I\'m prioritizing product features, starting with capturing various inputs: text, voice, photos, and different thought lengths. I\'m giving extra attention to a clean voice input UI.\n\n\n**Refining Input Capture**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best input capture method. Considering HTML5 recording with a micro-animated visualizer for voice, and robust photo integration, including drag-and-drop. I\'m prioritizing elegance and user-friendliness in these UI interactions.\n\n\n\n**Updating Data Structure**\n\nI\'m now revising the data structure for journal entries. I\'m incorporating a `cards` list within the `summary` to store \"Goal,\" \"Moment,\" \"Person,\" and \"Pattern\" entries. The existing schema has been checked and adapted. The `JournalEntry` interface now includes the `cards` array and `witnessReflection`. I am working on the data structure now.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Structure**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the database structure. The new `summary.cards` structure is really elegant! It keeps the raw journal data clean while beautifully deriving cards and connections. The database\'s `entries` collection is a perfect fit for this. I\'m excited by the gamification possibilities of dynamically tracking things like connections, unique cards, resolved questions, and revisiting old entries. I\'m exploring how to present this progress in a compelling \"My Story\" or \"Discover\" tab.\n\n\n**Designing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the interface design, specifically focusing on the \"My Story\" and \"Discover\" tabs. I envision \"My Story\" as a beautiful timeline showcasing structured cards with status badges. I\'m excited about the interactive \"Connections\" map and the \"Discover\" tab, which will present long-term patterns and insights. I am also modeling Threat Zones, making sure to include a Threat Summary Table. I\'m focusing on user experience, and have implemented threat modeling as a first step.\n\n\n**Securing System Components**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in security. I\'ve formulated strategies around the use of Firestore, and am restricting context in system prompts to mitigate prompt injections. Secure Firebase token validation before calling the API. I\'m also enforcing per-user paths in all Firestore rules and queries for complete user isolation, preventing any cross-tenant data access. No API keys are leaked, either; all processing is server-side with `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. I\'m also reviewing `/lib/context/JournalContext.tsx`, and the associated state structures, and making sure to include support for derived card structures. I am planning the integration of memory retention or the evolution of memories.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `/app/api/gemini/analyze/route.ts` to implement Sanjaya\'s distinct AI behavior rules. It will operate purely as an objective witness to the user\'s life story, avoiding motivational coaching or clinical diagnoses. It will extract lightweight structured cards (`Thought`, `Idea`, `Question`, `Decision`, `Goal`, `Moment`, `Person`, `Pattern`), synthesize an elegant witness reflection, and detect relationships to previous entries."
    thinking_duration {
