  planner_response {
    response: "### Agentic Threat Modeling Summary\n\n| Threat Zone | Identified Risks | Countermeasures & Architectural Mitigations |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Input Surfaces** | Untrusted multi-modal payloads, malformed JSON, prompt injection via raw user text/transcripts, unexpected fields in request bodies. | Strict schema parsing with defensive defaults; null-safe object destructuring; sanitization stripping `undefined` properties before database ingestion. |\n| **2. Planning & Reasoning** | Prompt injection attempting to alter Sanjaya persona, system instruction leakage, unsolicited advice/psychological diagnosis generation. | Strict system instructions enforcing objective mirror role; multi-level conversational constraints; LLM output constrained to schema-validated JSON where structured memory is required. |\n| **3. Tool & Engine Execution** | Privilege escalation, arbitrary data deletion, unauthorized state mutation. | Token verification at every API boundary (`verifyUserToken`); owner-bound identity matching against Firestore paths (`request.auth.uid == userId`); explicit whitelist of editable state fields. |\n| **4. Memory & State** | Cross-tenant data leakage, session hijacking, state corruption due to unhandled undefined attributes, memory inconsistency. | Database-level Firestore security rules enforcing complete isolation per authenticated user (`/users/{userId}/*`); `sanitizePayload` stripping `undefined`; reconciliation engine preserving historical transition periods (`validFrom`, `validTo`). |\n| **5. Inter-System Communication** | Server-side API key leakage, token sniffing, Gemini API exhaustion/outage (`429`, `503`). | Zero client-side API keys; all Gemini calls routed through server API endpoints; multi-model resilient fallback ladder (`gemini-2.5-flash` \342\206\222 `gemini-2.5-pro` \342\206\222 `gemini-3.6-flash` \342\206\222 `gemini-3.7-flash`). |\n\n---\n\n### Backend & Memory Layer Implementation\n\nThe **Personal Memory Engine** backend has been implemented:\n\n1. **Intermediate Blueprint & Hardened Firestore Rules**:\n   - Registered all core autobiographical entity models in `firebase-blueprint.json` (`CaptureSession`, `Episode`, `Entity`, `Relationship`, `Emotion`, `MemoryState`, `Learning`, `Pattern`, `MemoryProvenance`).\n   - Deployed owner-isolated, production-grade security rules in `firestore.rules`.\n\n2. **Core Memory Engine Modules (`/lib/memory-engine/`)**:\n   - **`types.ts`**: Complete type definitions for episodic memories, entities, temporal validity, emotion attribution, internal states, learnings, patterns, and provenance chains.\n   - **`extractor.ts`**: Schema-guided extraction engine powered by Gemini with temporal interpretation and emotional attribution (distinguishing user-felt emotions vs. user-observed emotions).\n   - **`store.ts`**: Firestore persistence layer with defensive payload sanitization (`sanitizePayload`) and user-scoped data access.\n   - **`reconciliation.ts`**: Graph reconciler that resolves aliases, updates entity timelines, and preserves relationship history using `validFrom` / `validTo` without overwriting historical facts.\n   - **`retriever.ts`**: Hybrid retrieval engine combining multi-hop entity relations, keyword relevance, recency decay, and active internal states.\n   - **`reflection.ts`**: Three-level conversational mirror that adheres strictly to *\"The system remembers more than it says\"*, completely avoiding unsolicited advice or diagnostic labels.\n   - **`maintenance.ts`**: Background pattern miner and duplicate entity resolution service.\n\n3. **RESTful API Endpoints (`/app/api/v1/...`)**:\n   - `POST /api/v1/capture`: Ingests multi-modal captures, triggers background extraction, and reconciles the memory graph.\n   - `GET /api/v1/captures`: Lists recent capture sessions.\n   - `GET /api/v1/capture/[id]`: Fetches a capture session and its extraction status.\n   - `POST /api/v1/capture/media`: Ingests and links media assets (images, audio, screenshots, documents).\n   - `GET /api/v1/entities` & `POST /api/v1/entities`: Queries and creates persistent entities.\n   - `GET /api/v1/entities/[id]`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`: Manages entity metadata, aliases, relationships, and history.\n   - `GET /api/v1/entities/[id]/timeline`: Returns the chronological autobiographical episode timeline for any person or entity.\n   - `GET /api/v1/relationships/[id]`: Retrieves relationship validity history.\n   - `POST /api/v1/retrieve`: Retrieves compact memory context for conversational grounding.\n   - `POST /api/v1/reflect`: Generates grounded conversational reflections without unsolicited directives.\n   - `PATCH /api/v1/memories/[id]` & `DELETE`: Allows user corrections and auditing.\n   - `POST /api/v1/maintenance`: Runs background candidate pattern detection and duplicate identification.\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Functional Walkthrough & Test Suite\n\nThe following test cases cover the complete lifecycle of memory ingestion, reconciliation, retrieval, and reflection:\n\n#### Test Case 1: Unified Capture Ingestion & Extraction\n1. **Action**: Send a `POST` request to `/api/v1/capture` with an authorization token and the payload:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"content\": \"Had dinner yesterday with Alex at Blue Hill. Alex seemed stressed about the new funding round. I realized I need to set clearer boundaries on my evening hours.\",\n     \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\"\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Verification**:\n   - Status code is `200 OK`.\n   - `extractedBundle.entities` contains `Alex` (`PERSON`, confidence $\\ge 0.8$) and `Blue Hill` (`PLACE`).\n   - `extractedBundle.episodes` contains a meal episode resolved to yesterday\'s date.\n   - `extractedBundle.emotions` attributes `stress` with `subjectName: \"Alex\"` (not the user).\n   - `extractedBundle.learnings` contains the realization about evening work boundaries.\n\n#### Test Case 2: Relationship Evolution & Historical Transition\n1. **Action**: Capture `\"Alex joined Stripe as engineering lead last month\"` followed later by `\"Alex moved to Anthropic as research engineer today\"`.\n2. **Verification**:\n   - The initial `works_at` relationship for Stripe is marked with `status: \"historical\"` and `validTo` set to today\'s timestamp.\n   - A new `works_at` relationship for Anthropic is created with `status: \"active\"` and `validFrom` set to today\'s timestamp.\n   - Querying `GET /api/v1/entities/{alex_id}/timeline` displays both experiences in reverse chronological order.\n\n#### Test Case 3: Grounded Conversational Reflection\n1. **Action**: Send a `POST` request to `/api/v1/reflect` with message: `\"I\'m feeling hesitant about scheduling this weekend\'s catchup with Alex.\"`\n2. **Verification**:\n   - The response mirrors the user\'s hesitation naturally without quoting database records directly.\n   - No unsolicited advice (e.g., \"You should reach out\") or diagnostic labels are present.\n   - Response utilizes the silent context of past stress and boundary goals to frame thoughtful questions.\n\n#### Test Case 4: Background Pattern Mining & Deduplication\n1. **Action**: Send a `POST` request to `/api/v1/maintenance` with `action: \"all\"`.\n2. **Verification**:\n   - Discovered candidate patterns are returned with supporting episode IDs and stored in `/users/{userId}/patterns/`.\n   - Duplicate entity candidates (exact name matches or alias intersections) are surfaced for user review."
    modified_response: "### Agentic Threat Modeling Summary\n\n| Threat Zone | Identified Risks | Countermeasures & Architectural Mitigations |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Input Surfaces** | Untrusted multi-modal payloads, malformed JSON, prompt injection via raw user text/transcripts, unexpected fields in request bodies. | Strict schema parsing with defensive defaults; null-safe object destructuring; sanitization stripping `undefined` properties before database ingestion. |\n| **2. Planning & Reasoning** | Prompt injection attempting to alter Sanjaya persona, system instruction leakage, unsolicited advice/psychological diagnosis generation. | Strict system instructions enforcing objective mirror role; multi-level conversational constraints; LLM output constrained to schema-validated JSON where structured memory is required. |\n| **3. Tool & Engine Execution** | Privilege escalation, arbitrary data deletion, unauthorized state mutation. | Token verification at every API boundary (`verifyUserToken`); owner-bound identity matching against Firestore paths (`request.auth.uid == userId`); explicit whitelist of editable state fields. |\n| **4. Memory & State** | Cross-tenant data leakage, session hijacking, state corruption due to unhandled undefined attributes, memory inconsistency. | Database-level Firestore security rules enforcing complete isolation per authenticated user (`/users/{userId}/*`); `sanitizePayload` stripping `undefined`; reconciliation engine preserving historical transition periods (`validFrom`, `validTo`). |\n| **5. Inter-System Communication** | Server-side API key leakage, token sniffing, Gemini API exhaustion/outage (`429`, `503`). | Zero client-side API keys; all Gemini calls routed through server API endpoints; multi-model resilient fallback ladder (`gemini-2.5-flash` \342\206\222 `gemini-2.5-pro` \342\206\222 `gemini-3.6-flash` \342\206\222 `gemini-3.7-flash`). |\n\n---\n\n### Backend & Memory Layer Implementation\n\nThe **Personal Memory Engine** backend has been implemented:\n\n1. **Intermediate Blueprint & Hardened Firestore Rules**:\n   - Registered all core autobiographical entity models in `firebase-blueprint.json` (`CaptureSession`, `Episode`, `Entity`, `Relationship`, `Emotion`, `MemoryState`, `Learning`, `Pattern`, `MemoryProvenance`).\n   - Deployed owner-isolated, production-grade security rules in `firestore.rules`.\n\n2. **Core Memory Engine Modules (`/lib/memory-engine/`)**:\n   - **`types.ts`**: Complete type definitions for episodic memories, entities, temporal validity, emotion attribution, internal states, learnings, patterns, and provenance chains.\n   - **`extractor.ts`**: Schema-guided extraction engine powered by Gemini with temporal interpretation and emotional attribution (distinguishing user-felt emotions vs. user-observed emotions).\n   - **`store.ts`**: Firestore persistence layer with defensive payload sanitization (`sanitizePayload`) and user-scoped data access.\n   - **`reconciliation.ts`**: Graph reconciler that resolves aliases, updates entity timelines, and preserves relationship history using `validFrom` / `validTo` without overwriting historical facts.\n   - **`retriever.ts`**: Hybrid retrieval engine combining multi-hop entity relations, keyword relevance, recency decay, and active internal states.\n   - **`reflection.ts`**: Three-level conversational mirror that adheres strictly to *\"The system remembers more than it says\"*, completely avoiding unsolicited advice or diagnostic labels.\n   - **`maintenance.ts`**: Background pattern miner and duplicate entity resolution service.\n\n3. **RESTful API Endpoints (`/app/api/v1/...`)**:\n   - `POST /api/v1/capture`: Ingests multi-modal captures, triggers background extraction, and reconciles the memory graph.\n   - `GET /api/v1/captures`: Lists recent capture sessions.\n   - `GET /api/v1/capture/[id]`: Fetches a capture session and its extraction status.\n   - `POST /api/v1/capture/media`: Ingests and links media assets (images, audio, screenshots, documents).\n   - `GET /api/v1/entities` & `POST /api/v1/entities`: Queries and creates persistent entities.\n   - `GET /api/v1/entities/[id]`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`: Manages entity metadata, aliases, relationships, and history.\n   - `GET /api/v1/entities/[id]/timeline`: Returns the chronological autobiographical episode timeline for any person or entity.\n   - `GET /api/v1/relationships/[id]`: Retrieves relationship validity history.\n   - `POST /api/v1/retrieve`: Retrieves compact memory context for conversational grounding.\n   - `POST /api/v1/reflect`: Generates grounded conversational reflections without unsolicited directives.\n   - `PATCH /api/v1/memories/[id]` & `DELETE`: Allows user corrections and auditing.\n   - `POST /api/v1/maintenance`: Runs background candidate pattern detection and duplicate identification.\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Functional Walkthrough & Test Suite\n\nThe following test cases cover the complete lifecycle of memory ingestion, reconciliation, retrieval, and reflection:\n\n#### Test Case 1: Unified Capture Ingestion & Extraction\n1. **Action**: Send a `POST` request to `/api/v1/capture` with an authorization token and the payload:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"content\": \"Had dinner yesterday with Alex at Blue Hill. Alex seemed stressed about the new funding round. I realized I need to set clearer boundaries on my evening hours.\",\n     \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\"\n   }\n   ```\n2. **Verification**:\n   - Status code is `200 OK`.\n   - `extractedBundle.entities` contains `Alex` (`PERSON`, confidence $\\ge 0.8$) and `Blue Hill` (`PLACE`).\n   - `extractedBundle.episodes` contains a meal episode resolved to yesterday\'s date.\n   - `extractedBundle.emotions` attributes `stress` with `subjectName: \"Alex\"` (not the user).\n   - `extractedBundle.learnings` contains the realization about evening work boundaries.\n\n#### Test Case 2: Relationship Evolution & Historical Transition\n1. **Action**: Capture `\"Alex joined Stripe as engineering lead last month\"` followed later by `\"Alex moved to Anthropic as research engineer today\"`.\n2. **Verification**:\n   - The initial `works_at` relationship for Stripe is marked with `status: \"historical\"` and `validTo` set to today\'s timestamp.\n   - A new `works_at` relationship for Anthropic is created with `status: \"active\"` and `validFrom` set to today\'s timestamp.\n   - Querying `GET /api/v1/entities/{alex_id}/timeline` displays both experiences in reverse chronological order.\n\n#### Test Case 3: Grounded Conversational Reflection\n1. **Action**: Send a `POST` request to `/api/v1/reflect` with message: `\"I\'m feeling hesitant about scheduling this weekend\'s catchup with Alex.\"`\n2. **Verification**:\n   - The response mirrors the user\'s hesitation naturally without quoting database records directly.\n   - No unsolicited advice (e.g., \"You should reach out\") or diagnostic labels are present.\n   - Response utilizes the silent context of past stress and boundary goals to frame thoughtful questions.\n\n#### Test Case 4: Background Pattern Mining & Deduplication\n1. **Action**: Send a `POST` request to `/api/v1/maintenance` with `action: \"all\"`.\n2. **Verification**:\n   - Discovered candidate patterns are returned with supporting episode IDs and stored in `/users/{userId}/patterns/`.\n   - Duplicate entity candidates (exact name matches or alias intersections) are surfaced for user review."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788252764
      nanos: 300866816
