    thinking: "**Analyzing Journal Input**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on `JournalContext.tsx` and how it interacts with Firestore for entries and memories. The key is to integrate the user\'s input with the journal in a nuanced manner. I\'m considering ways to prevent the journal from blindly accepting every statement as fact, so it has to assess the statements more deeply.\n\n\n**Refining Clarification Approach**\n\nI\'m now refining the clarification strategies. Instead of aggressive fact-checking, I\'m aiming for a more thoughtful, friendly interaction. Specifically, I\'m considering different scenarios. For example, when there\'s ambiguity (like multiple \"Sams\"), a gentle probe is needed to ensure accurate memory linking. If there\'s an entity mismatch, the system should offer a contextual suggestion to prompt for correction. Temporal inconsistencies require historical validity checks before triggering a clarification request. This will integrate into the pipeline I\'m designing.\n\n\n**Updating Memory Pipeline**\n\nI\'ve just refined the memory update pipeline to manage corrections. I\'m focusing on handling corrections while preserving provenance. For instance, when a user corrects a date, the active memory updates, but the original capture remains. Now, I\'m integrating confidence levels, and the UI contract and API for the clarification candidates that the user will interact with, with the goal of testing all proposed cases. The epistemic separation of `USER_SAID`, `SYSTEM_KNOWS`, etc., is also fully defined.\n\n\n**Defining Memory Structure**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the file structure for the memory engine, focusing on `/lib/memory-engine/`. I\'m fleshing out the `types.ts` file. I\'m building out enums and types, like `EpistemicSource` and `ClarificationType`, which are pivotal for managing different knowledge states and the types of clarification needed. The goal is a cleanly modular and robust memory system.\n\n\n**Defining Clarification Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the data structures for clarifications, specifically in the `types.ts` file. I\'m fleshing out the `Clarification` and `ExtractedBundle` types. We\'ll be using epistemic status, confidence levels, and significance to determine clarification priority. We will need to define `ClarificationStatus`. The `ExtractedBundle` will include entities, relationships, episodes, etc.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `firebase-blueprint.json` to inspect the blueprint configuration."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 803442035
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
