    response: "I will create `/lib/memory-engine/consistency.ts` implementing the Consistency & Clarification layer."
    thinking: "**Constructing Consistency Layer**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `/lib/memory-engine/consistency.ts` file. I\'m carefully reviewing the initial prompt\'s requirements for the Consistency & Clarification Engine. Specifically, I\'m focusing on how the journal shouldn\'t treat every statement equally, and will test to ensure that is the case.\n\n\n**Analyzing Ambiguity and Inconsistency**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on how to identify ambiguous, incorrect, or inconsistent statements within the user\'s input. The goal is to develop a robust system to handle these cases. I\'m exploring methods to flag ambiguous statements (like multiple \"Sams\") when they impact memory. I\'m also working on detecting potentially incorrect information, comparing it with world knowledge, and checking temporal inconsistencies. I want to avoid false positives by ignoring valid historical transitions and minor time discrepancies.\n\n\n**Refining Correction Mechanisms**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the system should handle user corrections, prioritizing the user\'s input. When a user provides a direct correction (like the Rahul example), the system will update active memory while preserving the original statement\'s provenance. I\'m also working on a confidence-based interruption mechanism, ensuring that clarifications are sought only when there are significant contradictions or high-confidence issues. I am emphasizing a tone of friendly recall, not an overly critical fact-checker, in all system interactions, and implementing epistemic separation to ensure the user retains final authority. I will now integrate `ConsistencyEngine` into `/lib/memory-engine/consistency.ts`, focusing on deterministic heuristics and model-based reasoning for optimal performance and accuracy, and I am starting the design of `ConsistencyEngine`, where it will take raw input, an extracted bundle, user ID and a store as input. My next step will be querying existing entities.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/lib/memory-engine/consistency.ts` implementing the Consistency & Clarification layer."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 303942297
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
